  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to water security in West African countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water is becoming increasingly scarce in West African countries, which often already suffer from a structural shortage of water infrastructure. In some regions, like the Sahel, this lack of access to water has been exacerbated by conflict or insecurity. Addressing water management, including water-related disasters, is further complicated due to transboundary elements, which demands cross-national solutions. Major climate related risks to water supply faced by the region are droughts, floods and erosion. UNESCO&apos;s IHP activities are meant to help address some of these water-related challenges and would be utilized to address them</narrative>
  </description>
